---
import DocLayout from "../layouts/DocLayout.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "channels", label: "Where to reach us" },
  { id: "bugs", label: "Reporting a bug" },
  { id: "private", label: "Private matters" },
];
---

<DocLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Get in touch with the Free JSON Toolkit project: report bugs, request tools, or reach out privately. Built in the open, on GitHub."
  eyebrow="Contact"
  lede="No support queue, no ticket system — just the open channels where the project actually lives."
  toc={toc}
  updated="2026-07-30"
>
  <section class="doc-section" id="channels">
    <h2>Where to reach us</h2>
    <p>
      The fastest, most useful way to reach the project is on GitHub. Bug reports, feature requests,
      and questions about the roadmap all belong there, in the open, where the next person with the
      same question can find the answer.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/pelomehuliyo/freejsontoolkit.com/issues"
        >Open or browse issues on GitHub →</a
      >
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="bugs">
    <h2>Reporting a bug</h2>
    <p>A bug report we can act on usually includes four things:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The tool and the URL you were on.</li>
      <li>What you did, step by step.</li>
      <li>What you expected, versus what actually happened.</li>
      <li>
        Any <strong>red error</strong> from the browser console (F12 → Console) — a single line of it
        is often the whole fix.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because every tool runs locally, your browser and its version matter too — include them if you
      can.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="private">
    <h2>Private matters</h2>
    <p>
      For anything that shouldn't be public — a security concern, a privacy question, or something
      personal — reach out by email and it will stay between us.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:contact@freejsontoolkit.com">contact@freejsontoolkit.com</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Note that, by design, we have no record of the data you process, so we can't retrieve or
      delete a copy of it on our side — there simply isn't one. The privacy page explains exactly
      what is and isn't stored.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocLayout>
